{
  "name": "Reckons \u2014 Note Drain (local poller)",
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": false,
    "description": "Two endpoints the user's own machine calls: GET drains buffered notes, POST acks the ones it wrote to disk. Delivery is at-least-once by design."
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Two endpoints, deliberately\n\n**GET /webhook/reckons-notes-drain** returns buffered notes and deletes NOTHING.\n\n**POST /webhook/reckons-notes-ack** `{ids:[...]}` deletes the rows the poller has already written to disk.\n\n## Why not one call\n\nA single get-and-delete loses a note whenever the poller dies between n8n's delete and the local write \u2014 and a dictated note lost is unrecoverable. Splitting it means the same crash produces a DUPLICATE instead, which is harmless: pending rows carry deterministic ids and the app dedupes on import.\n\nAt-least-once is the only correct choice for capture. Never trade a harmless duplicate for a silent loss.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "sticky",
      "name": "Read me first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -460,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "GET",
        "path": "reckons-notes-drain",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "authentication": "headerAuth",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "hookget",
      "name": "Drain requested",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        80,
        120
      ],
      "webhookId": "reckons-notes-drain"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "get",
        "tableName": "reckons_notes",
        "returnAll": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "rows",
      "name": "Read buffered notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        300,
        120
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ ok: true, rows: $input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(r => r && r.id) }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "sendrows",
      "name": "Return rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        520,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "reckons-notes-ack",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "authentication": "headerAuth",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "hookack",
      "name": "Ack received",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        80,
        380
      ],
      "webhookId": "reckons-notes-ack"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One item per id the poller confirmed it wrote to disk. Anything not acked stays\n// buffered and is delivered again next poll \u2014 which is the point.\nconst ids = $input.first().json.body?.ids;\nif (!Array.isArray(ids)) return [];\nreturn ids.filter(id => id !== undefined && id !== null).map(id => ({ json: { id } }));"
      },
      "id": "fanout",
      "name": "One per id",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        300,
        380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "deleteRows",
        "tableName": "reckons_notes",
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "id",
              "condition": "eq",
              "keyValue": "={{ $json.id }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "del",
      "name": "Drop acked rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        520,
        380
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ ok: true, deleted: $input.all().length }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "ackok",
      "name": "Confirm ack",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        740,
        380
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Drain requested": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Read buffered notes",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Read buffered notes": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Return rows",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Ack received": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "One per id",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "One per id": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Drop acked rows",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Drop acked rows": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Confirm ack",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "pinData": {}
}
